 "response": "**Gedebren's current budget is $2,224K.**\n\n1. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget to $1,710K. No later record sets an absolute figure, so every other budget change is an increase or decrease.\n2. **Ignored records:** Messages not from the Finance Office are ignored. So are Finance Office records that don't change the budget, such as invoices, receipts and room changes.\n3. **Withdrawals:** For each withdrawal chain, I worked from the last withdrawal backwards. A withdrawal counts only if nothing active withdraws it. Examples:\n   - #0005 is withdrawn. #0009 withdraws it, #0039 withdraws #0009, and #0474 withdraws #0039. With #0039 cancelled, #0009 is active again.\n   - #0006 stands. #0667 cancels #0063, which revives #0043. #0043 cancels #0024, so #0024's withdrawal of #0006 never takes effect.\n   - #0465 stands withdrawn. #1574 withdraws it, and nothing withdraws #1574.\n4. **Final total:** I then applied every remaining budget change in record order, ending at #1600 (+$60K). I did this by hand across about 1,600 records, so small arithmetic slips are possible, though I checked each chain.\n\nANSWER: $2224K",
